---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} automatically sends the following information to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink>: app use,
      purchases, crashes, performance, app and device details, accessibility
      settings, color scheme, language, layout direction, and region. We use
      this information to understand how {APP_NAME} is used and improve the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      It also sends a one-way hash of a random ID made for that installation.
      The ID stays the same until the app's data is reset or the app is
      uninstalled.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can stop future analytics in the app's settings. This does not remove
      information already sent. We do not set a fixed deletion date for past
      analytics. Because we cannot connect those records to your name or email
      address, we cannot find and delete one person's analytics.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck will provide the same or equal protection for analytics data
      as this policy and Apple's rules require.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us a content report, the email includes your reason, the
      round ID, app version, and build number. The report comes from your email
      account, so we receive that email address. A drawing is included only if
      you choose to attach it. We use this information to review the reported
      content.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep report emails in our support inbox until you ask us to remove your
      report by emailing <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address used to send it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No other party collects personally identifiable information about your
      online activities over time and across different websites or online
      services when you use {APP_NAME}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will post material changes to this policy on this page.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
